===Film===
Lake Wakatipu doubled as the Scottish [[Loch Ness]] in the 2007 film ''[[The Water Horse: Legend of the Deep]]''.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://entertainment.howstuffworks.com/water-horse3.htm |title=Inside 'The Water Horse' |access-date=7 July 2008 |last=Miller |first=Gerri |date=21 December 2007 |publisher=HowStuffWorks, Inc. }}</ref>

The lake was a backdrop for several scenes in ''[[The Lord of the Rings: The Fellowship of the Ring]]'', including [[Minor places in Middle-earth|Amon Hen]].

===Television===
Lake Wakatipu is the titular lake in the murder mystery television series ''[[Top of the Lake]]'' (2013).<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/magazine-23686419|title=''Top of the Lake'': Is New Zealand's greatest actor New Zealand itself?|author=Lane, Megan |work=BBC News Magazine|date =17 August 2013}}</ref>

==Sports==
===Swimming===
The first person to swim the length of the lake was Ben Campbell-Macdonald in 2012. The 81&nbsp;km solo wetsuit swim from Kingston on the lake's southern point to Glenorchy took 18.5 hours.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Lacy |first1=Judith |title=Southern Everest knocked off |url=https://www.stuff.co.nz/manawatu-standard/your-manawatu/tribune/6458663/Southern-Everest-knocked-off |work=Stuff |date=21 February 2012 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Dodgshun |first1=Joe |title=First person to swim Lake Wakatipu |url=https://www.odt.co.nz/regions/queenstown/first-person-swim-lake-wakatipu |work=[[Otago Daily Times]] |date=7 February 2012 |language=en}}</ref>

